r!!!","artist":"The Whomping Willows","year":2010,"weight":3,"yt":"tv1pnG9zyh4","src":"rym","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":64027302966167,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Wizard Rock","rank":33,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Harry Potter Inspiration","body":"Wizard rock is a subgenre composed of bands entirely inspired by the Harry Potter series of books and films. \"A whole bunch of bands inspired by Harry Potter.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Nerd Rock","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h6snk0m4200"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Inspiration and Festival","body":"Wizard Rock is a subgenre of nerd rock entirely inspired by the Harry Potter book series. The scene is sufficiently large and dedicated to have its own festival, which is known as \"Wrockstock.\" \"There was Wizard Rock, a whole bunch of bands inspired by Harry Potter. That scene is big enough to have its own festival, which they call Rockstock, which is spelled with a silent W at the beginning.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"History of Nerd Rock","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8lQv8eMJ868"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Rockstock Festival","body":"The wizard rock scene is substantial enough to host its own dedicated festival, known as \"Rockstock,\" which famously includes a silent 'W' at the beginning of its spelling. \"That scene is big enough to have its own festival, which they call Rockstock, which is spelled with a silent W at the beginning.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Nerd Rock","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h6snk0m4200"}]}]}